  "term": "megalencephaly",
  "definition": "Megalencephaly is a congenital abnormality in which the occipitofrontal head circumference is more than two standard deviations above the average for the person’s age. It can occur with hydrocephalus, subdural effusion, arachnoid cysts, or as part of a genetic condition.",
